{"timestamp": "2025-07-28T10:16:15.076069", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Convert primitive name to its corresponding index\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Initialize an empty list to store the actions needed to collect the primitive\n  actions_to_take = []\n\n  def move_towards_target(target_pos):\n    \"\"\"Move towards a target position.\"\"\"\n    current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n    delta_x = target_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n    delta_y = target_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n\n    # Move horizontally first\n    if delta_x > 0:\n      actions_to_take.extend([env.world.N_RIGHT] * abs(delta_x))\n    elif delta_x < 0:\n      actions_to_take.extend([env.world.N_LEFT] * abs(delta_x))\n\n    # Then move vertically\n    if delta_y > 0:\n      actions_to_take.extend([env.world.N_DOWN] * abs(delta_y))\n    elif delta_y < 0:\n      actions_to_take.extend([env.world.N_UP] * abs(delta_y))\n\n  def find_and_collect_primitive():\n    \"\"\"Find and collect the primitive in the environment.\"\"\"\n    grid = env._current_state.grid\n    width, height, _ = grid.shape\n\n    # Search for the primitive in the grid\n    for y in range(height):\n      for x in range(width):\n        if grid[x, y, primitive_index] > 0:\n          target_pos = (x, y)\n          move_towards_target(target_pos)\n          actions_to_take.append(env.world.USE)  # Action to collect the primitive\n\n  find_and_collect_primitive()\n  return actions_to_take", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
